---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import Breadcrumbs from '../../components/Breadcrumbs.astro';
import { href } from '../../lib/data';
import { breadcrumbNode, pageGraph, webPageNode } from '../../lib/schema';

const title = 'HOA rules for parking an RV at home | RV Storage Prices';
const description =
  'Notes on association rules for an RV or boat kept at home. Florida, Nevada, Arizona, Texas, Georgia, and North Carolina each have a page. Not legal advice.';
const path = '/rules/';
const checked = '2026-11-19';
const crumbs = [
  { label: 'Home', path: '/' },
  { label: 'HOA rules', path },
];
const schema = pageGraph([
  webPageNode({ title, description, path, dateModified: checked }),
  breadcrumbNode(crumbs),
]);
---

<Base title={title} description={description} path={path} schema={schema}>
  <article class="wrap prose">
    <Breadcrumbs items={crumbs} />
    <h1>HOA rules for an RV or boat at home</h1>
    <p>
      These notes quote a statute and say what that sentence does not decide. They are not legal advice,
      and they are not a reading of your declaration, your city code, or a condominium document.
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <a href={href('/rules/florida/')}>Florida</a>. Section 720.3045 limits some bans on an RV or boat
        that is not visible from listed places.
      </li>
      <li>
        <a href={href('/rules/nevada/')}>Nevada</a>. NRS 116.350 allows reasonable restrictions on RV,
        watercraft, and trailer parking.
      </li>
      <li>
        <a href={href('/rules/arizona/')}>Arizona</a>. No statute found that sets an RV or boat parking
        rule for a planned community.
      </li>
      <li>
        <a href={href('/rules/texas/')}>Texas</a>. Section 209.015 mentions a recreational vehicle only
        inside an adjacent-lot definition, and only if the instrument already permits it.
      </li>
      <li>
        <a href={href('/rules/georgia/')}>Georgia</a>. No statute found that names an RV or boat parking
        rule for a property owners’ association.
      </li>
      <li>
        <a href={href('/rules/north-carolina/')}>North Carolina</a>. Chapter 47F has no section that names
        an RV or a boat.
      </li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      Each page was checked on November 19, 2026. A storage listing is a lot for hire. It is not a
      statement about driveway or association rules.
    </p>
  </article>
</Base>
